The expansion brief asks for forty-two municipalities across the Golden
Horseshoe. The fastest way to deliver that is a page per municipality from one
template with the place name substituted in, and it is the single most reliably
punished pattern in local search, for the good reason that every one of those
pages is the same page.

This repository has already been here. F-157 records fifteen of sixteen
service-area pages rendering one generic paragraph with a place name swapped in,
and CityContent still carries the rule stamped on it: EVERY field must be REAL —
invented detail is worse than none.

So the unit of expansion here is a RECORD, not a page. content/geo/markets.ts
holds all 49 markets — 43 in Ontario, 6 in New York — each with its corridor
membership, its coverage status, the sentence that can honestly be said about
serving it, and the date somebody confirmed that sentence. Twenty-seven of them
carry no local content and therefore no page; they are first-class entities all
the same: corridor members, API records, internal-link targets, and a computed
queue of what to write next. lib/geo/worthiness.ts decides publication from four
requirements — real local content, a dated operational confirmation, not a US
proxy, no cannibalisation of a parent municipality — and the advisory score
cannot override any of them, because a score that can override a truth
requirement eventually will.

That is not caution slowing the expansion down. It is what lets it run: adding
the next twenty municipalities is a data change, and the day one of them has
real content its page appears with metadata, schema, sitemap entry, internal
links and API record already correct.

THE LINE THE UNITED STATES MARKETS DO NOT CROSS

Buffalo, Niagara Falls NY, Amherst, Cheektowaga, Tonawanda and Lockport exist so
that someone on the American side of the river who owns an Ontario property can
find an Ontario company. That is the whole purpose. They are status us-proxy,
they are excluded from serviceAreaMarkets() by construction, and
scripts/verify-geo.mjs fails the build if the us() constructor assigns any other
status, if us-proxy joins OPERATIONAL_STATUSES, or if the service-area filter
loses its verified-municipality condition. The first regression test found that
the guard was reporting the status it assumed rather than the one the code
assigns — it now reads the constructor.

DISTRICTS ARE NOT CITIES

Etobicoke is part of Toronto; Ancaster, Dundas and Stoney Creek are part of
Hamilton. A district never reaches areaServed as a peer City node of the
municipality containing it, declares no corridors of its own (a corridor is a
drive between municipalities), and inherits membership through partOf. The guard
caught the first draft asserting both, which is how two lists that must agree
start disagreeing.

Also: /corridors and /corridors/[id] for the nine routes, /api/v1/markets —
which publishes its own content_queue and the reason each market has no page,
because that is a more falsifiable statement about coverage than any map —
/api/v1/corridors, 18 unit tests, sitemap, header and llms.txt entries, and no
coordinate, drive time or population figure anywhere: those are the fields a
template most wants filled and the ones most likely to be invented.

Corrects old-domain/EXECUTE.md: `vercel domains add` needs the project name.
Without it the apex is added to the team and attached to nothing — it prints
Success and changes nothing — and the www subdomain is refused outright.

